<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - CITY LODGE RAISES YR SHARE, DIV.</title>
<headline>TABLE - CITY LODGE RAISES YR SHARE, DIV.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - undiluted	     139.0	 vs 128.7</p>
<p>    - fully diluted	 104.2	 vs  97.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  53.0	 vs  48.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    37.47	vs  33.54</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    49.61	vs  45.04</p>
<p>    Tax			  13.92	vs  13.75</p>
<p>    Interest expense	 13.50	vs  13.33</p>
<p>    Turnover		  123.07	vs 108.68</p>
<p>Full name: City Lodge Hotels Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it would award capitalisation shares to shareholders registered on August 29. They would be issued in the ratio that the dividend bears to the issue price -- defined as the weighted average of its share price on the Johannesburg Stock Exchange for the three daysending September 25 -- discounted by 10 percent.</p>
<p>The company said it expected to achieve further earnings growth in the year ahead.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
